Subject: [PATCH] Android ADM: allow a caller supplied AudioRecord factory

This patch is intentionally tied to UPSTREAM_REVISION before application. It adds
an AudioRecordFactory interface to JavaAudioDeviceModule.Builder and passes it to
WebRtcAudioRecord. WebRtcAudioRecord calls the factory instead of setAudioSource;
SimpleRC's factory constructs AudioRecord with setAudioPlaybackCaptureConfig.

Required source changes at the fixed revision:

1. sdk/android/api/org/webrtc/audio/JavaAudioDeviceModule.java
   - public interface AudioRecordFactory { AudioRecord create(int sampleRate,
     int channelMask, int audioFormat, int bufferSize); }
   - Builder.setAudioRecordFactory(@Nullable AudioRecordFactory factory)
   - pass factory into WebRtcAudioRecord constructor
   - reject simultaneous setAudioSource and custom factory use

2. sdk/android/src/java/org/webrtc/audio/WebRtcAudioRecord.java
   - store the nullable factory
   - in createAudioRecordOnMOrHigher, call factory.create(...) when non-null
   - require returned AudioRecord STATE_INITIALIZED
   - do not enable microphone AEC/NS for custom factory input

3. SimpleRC patch adapter (compiled only in patched-AAR variant)
   - build AudioPlaybackCaptureConfiguration from current MediaProjection
   - match USAGE_MEDIA, USAGE_GAME and USAGE_UNKNOWN
   - create AudioRecord.Builder with PCM_16BIT and the negotiated format
   - call setAudioPlaybackCaptureConfig; never set MIC/VOICE_COMMUNICATION source

No binary patch has been generated. Exact line hunks must be produced after the
upstream revision is fixed, then reviewed with git apply --check before building.
